Hoist the batch-level GDN speculative-decode metadata out of the per-cache-group
builder (upstream vLLM PR #52297, backported to the pinned 0.27.1).

GDNAttentionMetadataBuilder.build() recomputed the same batch-level quantities --
the spec/non-spec masks, the decode/prefill/spec-decode split, the token index
permutation, the query_start_loc cumsums and the spec-row gather of
num_accepted_tokens -- once for every GDN kv-cache group in a step. None of it
depends on the group; only the block_table gathers do. This moves it into
compute_common_gdn_attn_metadata() in v1/worker/gpu/attn_utils.py, called once per
step from MambaHybridModelState.prepare_attn(), and passes the results into each
group's build() as keyword arguments.

Upstream measured build() at ~900us -> ~300us and +61% output tok/s at concurrency
1 on Qwen3.6-35B-A3B + DFlash on an H200. This is a CPU-side saving, so expect far
less on a bandwidth-bound consumer pair; see heterogeneous/README.md for what it
actually measured here.

Backport notes (0.27.1 differs from upstream main):
- 0.27.1 spells the no-spec guard as a single compound `if` and uses inline
  `~spec_sequence_masks_cpu` where main hoists it to non_spec_sequence_masks_cpu.
  The hoisted helper follows main; the two are behaviourally identical, verified
  over 4,002 random batches (pure-spec, mixed, all-prefill, no-spec and padded
  zero-length rows, num_spec in {1,2,3,4,7,15}) plus the no-spec and
  all-drafts-zero edge paths.
- The builder's `self.num_spec` and the `vllm_config.num_speculative_tokens` the
  helper is called with are the same value for MTP and DFlash; they can only
  diverge under diffusion_config, which this repo does not use.
- Apply order: after vllm-pr46994-mtp-pp.patch (both touch mamba_hybrid.py) and
  before zz-dflash2-pipeline-parallel.patch. The default patches/*.patch glob
  order already does this.

  patch -p1 -d venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vllm < vllm-pr52297-gdn-common-metadata.patch

